Lead Engineer Operating Model
This project also demonstrates how a Lead Data Systems Engineer would organize and execute a complex 
modernization effort during the first 90 days.

First 30 Days: Discovery & Baseline

* Identify system owners
* Confirm points of contact
* Review current-state architecture
* Gather source system documentation
* Confirm data access requirements
* Identify compliance concerns
* Build initial data inventory
* Create risk and issue log
* Establish communication cadence

Days 31–60: Validation & Design
* Define source-to-target mapping
* Document transformation rules
* Create validation scripts
* Build data quality checks
* Review report dependencies
* Identify legacy logic
* Define acceptance criteria
* Create test evidence templates
* Begin prototype database build

Days 61–90: Execution & Reporting
* Execute migration test cycles
* Validate source-to-target accuracy
* Build exception reports
* Create executive dashboard
* Document audit findings
* Finalize traceability matrix
* Present modernization results
* Recommend next-phase improvements

