## Example Data Validation Logic

```sql
-- Record Count Validation
SELECT 
    'Legacy_Source' AS system_name,
    COUNT(*) AS record_count
FROM legacy_customer_data

UNION ALL

SELECT 
    'Modernized_Target' AS system_name,
    COUNT(*) AS record_count
FROM target_customer_data;

```sql
-- Duplicate Detection
SELECT 
    customer_id,
    COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM target_customer_data
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

```sql
-- Missing Required Fields
SELECT 
    customer_id,
    customer_name,
    email_address,
    created_date
FROM target_customer_data
WHERE customer_name IS NULL
   OR email_address IS NULL
   OR created_date IS NULL;

Sample Audit Log Table
```sql
CREATE TABLE data_migration_audit_log (
    audit_id INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    process_name VARCHAR2(100),
    source_table VARCHAR2(100),
    target_table VARCHAR2(100),
    records_processed NUMBER,
    records_passed NUMBER,
    records_failed NUMBER,
    validation_status VARCHAR2(50),
    validation_message VARCHAR2(500),
    executed_by VARCHAR2(100),
    executed_date TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

